curl-fuzz_bufq.0001-no-syscalls.patch
Platform adaptation.

fuzz_bufq.cc of curl-fuzzer 4768d8de6f3209bb5dd761cd24ff7ccbfbb6b5b8 (sha256 b3caf628a0f010b9...), for the fuzz target
fuzz_bufq, as the OSS Verify proofs of fuzz_bufq build it (the result has sha256 296a1729698087b0...). On its first
call the harness built its reference
pattern with signal(SIGPIPE, SIG_IGN), an anonymous MAP_SHARED mmap and an mprotect to PROT_READ, three calls the
process model the statements are judged in declines. The patch makes the pattern a static const table in read-only
data, built at compile time, and removes the three calls and the two asserts that checked them.

--- a/fuzz_bufq.cc	2026-10-31 19:10:56.000000000 +0000
+++ b/fuzz_bufq.cc	2026-10-31 19:11:39.000000000 +0000
@@ -22,9 +22,7 @@
 
